<speak>That is helpful. My wife is happy to remind me that something arrived, but she does not want to become my filing clerk either. We have been married long enough for her to say that quite directly. She handles plenty of household arrangements already. I think I sometimes mistake being reminded for having completed the task. She says, 'There is a letter for you,' and in my mind I have already dealt with the letter because I acknowledged her. Then it is still sitting there days later. A folder labelled awaiting attention would be a small but useful reminder that acknowledgement is not the same as finishing.</speak>